"""A53 loader shim — a tiny AArch64 ELF that copies an R5 image into TCM and
releases R5-0 out of module reset. Enables SD-card boot without a full FSBL.

The complete build chain (Phase 10, //scripts/flash) turns this into a
BOOT.BIN via:

  1. `bazel build --config=rpu //apps/rpu/hello_world`       → R5 ELF
  2. `arm-none-eabi-objcopy -O binary`                       → raw R5 binary
  3. `aarch64-none-elf-objcopy -I binary -O elf64-littleaarch64 -B aarch64`
                                                             → embeddable .o
  4. Link .o + startup.S + main.c + memory.lds               → A53 loader ELF
  5. `bootgen -image scripts/flash/boot_a53.bif -arch zynqmp -o BOOT.BIN`

Sources are exposed as filegroups so the flash script can consume them
without having to embed a cc_binary that would fail during a plain
`bazel build //board/a53_loader/...` (the R5 image is not yet available).
"""

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

filegroup(
    name = "sources",
    srcs = [
        "startup.S",
        "main.c",
    ],
)

filegroup(
    name = "linker_script",
    srcs = ["memory.lds"],
)
